```

To apply this style, simply add the "centered-element" class to the element you want to center.

You can horizontally center an iframe using the following CSS code:

```CSS
iframe {
    display: block;
    margin-left: auto;
    margin-right: auto;
}
```
This code employs the auto value for the left and right margins to make them evenly split the available space and hence keeping the element centered. Also, the display property is set to block since iframe elements are inline by default, and inline elements do not accept margin-top and margin-bottom.
